<title>CANADA: Northern Telecom wins contract.</title>
<headline>Northern Telecom wins contract.</headline>
<dateline>TORONTO 1997-01-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Northern Telecom Ltd said on Wednesday it won a deal from MCI Communications Corp under which MCI would buy US$200 million in high-capacity transmission equipment from Nortel in 1997.</p>
<p>Products to be purchased under the contract included Nortel's S/DMS TransportNode OC-192, OC-48 and OC-12 systems, the DV-45 and DV-MPEG codecs for video transport and Nortel's network manager.</p>
<p>Nortel said it had a leading position in the world market for commercially deployed OC-48 and OC-192 high-capacity SONET transport networks.</p>
<p>((Reuters Toronto Bureau (416) 941-8100))</p>
